The traditional way to inspect such a running log
file is with the "tail" command on Unix, Mac OS X and
Linux -- you also get tail with Cygwin on Windows.

We wanted to stream the output for scalability in
case a physicist somewhere needed to run a gazillion
samples to estimate something to umpteen decimal places.

- Bob

