Dear list,

Andrew: I think this is a good idea; incidentally, I was running these examples (in my later posts) with seed=1.

Bob and Jiqiang: I got the above data and model to run on my machine as you did, with init set to zero. The errors in my later posts ("error occurred during calling the sampler; sampling not done") were caused by the test_grad=TRUE argument I passed to stan. When I remove that argument the model sampled fine. Include it and it aborts after the first sample. I'm not sure if this is the desired behaviour for that argument (I thought it printed all evaluations?).

In any case, it is the inits that were causing the original error I posted as you suspected. If inits are set to zero the model gets through the samples just fine (though I assume in this case I can't really use the Rhat values, since the initial values were not diffuse); if inits are set to random then the sampler fails with the error "Initialization failed after 100 attempts.  Try specifying initial values, reducing ranges of constrained values, or reparameterizing the model."

Thanks for all your help sorting this out. Any recommendations for how to proceed with these models? Set my own inits?

Best

Tom

