Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When test_grad is TRUE, Stan would just test the gradient evaluation using algorithmic differentiation vs. finite diff for the inits (that is, it would not conduct sampling).  However, in this case, it is not supposed to see the following

"error occurred during calling the sampler; sampling not done"

If you see it again, please let me know.

I think you could just go ahead using your own initial values to fit the model, it is absolutely fine.

--
Jiqiang

