On Wednesday, December 19, 2012 10:06:42 PM UTC-5, Will Morris wrote:
> Could someone please help me out with this runtime error (below) I am getting. Have tried to run this model (http://cl.ly/131S3n330Z1K, with data http://cl.ly/code/0G3z0o441S0E) on both a Mac and Linux with optimisation on and off. Both give this error I can't interpret. Stan (v-1.1.0) itself is working fine as I can run the example models without error.

This is our bug. You can work around it by 1) restricting xi be slightly positive as in

real<lower=0.000001> xi[3];

and by 2) moving the calculation of the rhos into a generated quantities block at the end instead of the transformed parameters block

generated quantities {
  real<lower=-1, upper=1> rho[3];
  rho[1] <- Sigma_B_raw[1, 2] / sqrt(Sigma_B_raw[1, 1] * Sigma_B_raw[2, 2]);
  rho[2] <- Sigma_B_raw[1, 3] / sqrt(Sigma_B_raw[1, 1] * Sigma_B_raw[3, 3]);
  rho[3] <- Sigma_B_raw[2, 3] / sqrt(Sigma_B_raw[2, 2] * Sigma_B_raw[3, 3]);
}

In addition, although this is largely unrelated to the bug, if you are going to specify a uniform (0,100) prior on xi, then you should specify an upper bound on xi's support, like

real<lower=0.000001, upper=100> xi[3];

in which case, you do not need to explicitly specify the uniform prior on xi in the model block.

With all that, your model seems to run, albeit painfully slowly. There is a lot of new stuff in the Stan manual for v1.1.0 on reparameterizing models like this in Chapter 13.

Ben

