> I am working on a regression model where I am using Cauchy priors for the coefficients. Since the built-in Cauchy function is quite slow, I am trying to refactor my code to express the Cauchy distribution as a ratio of two Normal distributions. However, the parser isnt allowing me to divide two vectors. Is the only way to do this to express the division as a an explicit loop over all the elements of the vector?

You need to use the "./" operator, which is documented on page 149 of the v1.1.0 manual.

> Are there any better ways of speeding up sampling from the Cauchy? Thanks in advance!

I'm not sure that the log-posterior will evaluate much faster, but you may get more efficient sampling and hence need fewer total samples to achieve a given number of effective samples.

Ben

