On 12/26/12 9:44 PM, Jianling Zhong wrote:
> you mean inv_scale <- exp(log(phi) - log(mu_k))?

Ah, right, what I meant to write was

    inv_scale <- exp(log(phi) - X_k * beta);

so you avoid the round trip of exp and log on the linear
basis X_k * beta.

It's probably fastest for now (that is, until we add alternative
parameterizations and vectorize negative_binomial) to follow Ben's
advice.

